// HumanLang all functions example

say "1. Text output"
say "Hello from HumanLang"
show "Show also prints text"
print "Print also works"

say "2. Remember values"
remember 10 as first number
remember 4 as second number
remember "Steven" as user name

say "3. Basic math"
calculate first number plus second number as addition,
calculate first number minus second number as subtraction,
calculate first number times second number as multiplication,
calculate first number divided by second number as division,
calculate first number modulo second number as remainder,
calculate first number to the power of second number as power,

say "4. Scientific math"
calculate the square root of first number as root,
calculate the sine of radians of 90 as sine value,
calculate the cosine of radians of 0 as cosine value,
calculate the tangent of radians of 45 as tangent value,
calculate the log of 1000 as base ten log,
calculate the natural log of e as natural log,
calculate the absolute value of -10 as positive value,
calculate the floor of 4.9 as floor value,
calculate the ceiling of 4.1 as ceiling value,
calculate the factorial of 5 as factorial value,
calculate the rounded value of 4.7 as rounded value,

say "5. Useful calculator helpers"
calculate average of first number and second number as average value,
calculate the maximum of first number and second number as biggest value,
calculate the minimum of first number and second number as smallest value,
calculate 10 percent of first number as percent value,

say "6. Conditions"
if first number is greater than second number:
    say "First number is bigger"
otherwise:
    say "Second number is bigger or equal"

say "7. Repeat"
repeat 3 times:
    say "HumanLang can repeat"

say "8. Lists"
make list "apples", "bananas" and "mangoes" as fruits
add "oranges" to fruits
for each fruit in fruits:
    say fruit
calculate length of fruits as fruit count,

say "9. Random, date, and time"
calculate random integer between 1 and 6 as dice roll,
calculate random number between 1 and 2 as random value,
remember current date as today
remember current time as now
say today
say now

say "10. Files"
write "HumanLang file output" to file "humanlang_output.txt"
append " works" to file "humanlang_output.txt"
read file "humanlang_output.txt" as file text
say file text
